  "tagline": "Rust vector search engine with rich payload filtering, quantization and a managed cloud.",
  "description": "Qdrant is an open-source vector database written in Rust, known for fast filtered search: payload indexes are integrated into its HNSW graph so restrictive filters do not wreck recall. It supports dense, sparse and multi-vector points, scalar/binary/product quantization, a universal Query API for hybrid fusion and re-ranking, and distributed sharding with replication. It runs comfortably from a single Docker container to large clusters, and Qdrant Cloud adds managed, hybrid (your Kubernetes) and private deployments. A strong default for self-hosted vector search.",
