  "strengths": [
    "Filter-aware HNSW keeps recall high under restrictive payload filters",
    "Dense, sparse and multi-vector (ColBERT) support with server-side fusion",
    "Scalar, binary and product quantization with on-disk storage",
    "Small, efficient Rust binary that is easy to self-host",
    "Managed, hybrid and private cloud options"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Full-text support is a filter index, not a BM25 search engine",
    "No joins or relational queries",
    "Distributed mode requires planning shard counts up front",
    "Enterprise features such as SSO are cloud-tier only"
  ],
